    {
      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Object Storage Options**\n\nOkay, I'm leaning toward Amazon S3 for this `upload_object.py` script. The popularity of S3, combined with the power of `boto3`, makes it a sensible choice. I'm focusing on incorporating clear provider identification in the code, so it's easily apparent which service is being used for object storage.\n\n\n**Initiating File Creation**\n\nOkay, I've started putting together the `upload_object.py` file. I'm leveraging `boto3` to handle the S3 interactions. I've included placeholders for credentials, bucket name, and object key. The goal is to make it adaptable, while clearly showcasing the S3 connection. Next step is refining the initial code block.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818018435,
          "start": 1789818015301
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9778e44001isCd4Y3FJApbQw",
      "message_id": "msg_0b97788cb001t07W4fLJ36U5eR",
      "session_id": "ses_f468877c3ffefWlFOZXOrmOTup",
      "time_created": 1789818015301,
      "time_updated": 1789818018435
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "vLK4t1jZhYFqzeIO",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef upload_object(bucket_name, object_name, file_path=None, data=None):\n    \"\"\"Uploads a file or byte stream to an S3 bucket.\n\n    :param bucket_name: Name of the S3 bucket\n    :param object_name: S3 object name. If using file_path, this will be the name of the file in S3.\n    :param file_path: Path to the file to upload (optional)\n    :param data: Byte stream to upload (optional)\n    :return: True if object was uploaded, else False\n    \"\"\"\n    s3_client = boto3.client(\n        's3',\n        aws_access_key_id=os.environ.get(\"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\"),\n        aws_secret_access_key=os.environ.get(\"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\"),\n        region_name=os.environ.get(\"AWS_REGION\")\n    )\n\n    try:\n        if file_path:\n            s3_client.upload_file(file_path, bucket_name, object_name)\n            print(f\"File {file_path} uploaded to {bucket_name}/{object_name}\")\n        elif data is not None:\n            s3_client.put_object(Bucket=bucket_name, Key=object_name, Body=data)\n            print(f\"Byte stream uploaded to {bucket_name}/{object_name}\")\n        else:\n            print(\"Either file_path or data must be provided.\")\n            return False\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error uploading object: {e}\")\n        return False\n    return True\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Example Usage:\n    # Set your AWS credentials as environment variables:\n    # AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, AWS_REGION\n\n    # To upload a file:\n    # with open(\"my_local_file.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n    #     f.write(\"This is a test file.\")\n    # upload_object(\"your-s3-bucket-name\", \"remote_file.txt\", file_path=\"my_local_file.txt\")\n\n    # To upload a byte stream:\n    # byte_data = b\"This is a byte stream content.\"\n    # upload_object(\"your-s3-bucket-name\", \"remote_byte_stream.txt\", data=byte_data)\n",
            "filePath": "upload_object.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
